300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (The project titled "College Election Online Voting System" aims to design and develop a secure, efficient, and user-friendly web-based application that facilitates the digital conduct of student elections within a college environment. Traditional voting methods used in colleges, which involve ballot papers and manual vote counting, are often time-consuming, prone to human error, and susceptible to malpractices )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (This project proposes an online voting platform that allows eligible students to cast their votes securely through a digital interface using unique login credentials. The system ensures one-person-one-vote validation, data encryption for secure transmission, and real-time vote tallying to deliver instant and accurate results. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (The platform consists of key modules such as admin management, voter authentication, candidate listing, voting process, and result generation. The admin has privileges to manage elections, register candidates, and monitor the system, while authenticated students can log in to vote during the election window. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (The system is developed using technologies like HTML, CSS, JavaScript for the frontend, and PHP or Python with MySQL for the back-end, and follows a structured software development life cycle. By automating the voting process, the proposed system enhances transparency, reduces administrative workload, and ensures fair election procedures. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
