344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Manual voting with a secure web/mobile platform. It allows students to vote remotely through verified login using student IDs and OTP or biometric authentication. The system ensures vote privacy, integrity, and transparency using encryption and secure databases. Administrators can manage candidates, schedule elections, and view real-time progress. Compared to traditional methods, it reduces errors, saves time, and enhances accessibility. The system can also integrate blockchain for added security, ensuring a modern, efficient, and trustworthy election process. The College Election Online Voting System aims to digitize student elections by replacing. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (2)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 207 0 R
/T (1. INTRODUCTION )
/E (1. INTRODUCTION )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (The College Election Online Voting System is developed to provide a secure, transparent, and efficient platform for conducting student elections. Traditional paper-based voting is often time-consuming, prone to errors, and lacks real-time result generation. This system overcomes those challenges by using a web-based interface where students can log in securely, view candidate details, and cast their votes electronically. It ensures confidentiality, prevents duplicate voting, and automatically counts votes, providing quick and accurate results. This project aims to promote digital literacy, save time, and bring fairness to the election process. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (Furthermore, it reduces manual effort and promotes eco-friendly digital practices by eliminating paper ballots. The system enhances student participation and trust by ensuring fair, tamper-proof elections with instant result publication. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
